fix(gmail-labeler): round 2 - readonly planning client, --auth message, undo gate, revoked-token exit

Review round 2, three blockers + two small:

1. DRY-RUN BREAKS ON TODAY'S TOKEN: the planning client (dry-run AND the
   plan phase of --apply) is now built with [GMAIL_SCOPE] readonly ONLY -
   _labeler_client(modify=False). Only the write clients (apply, undo,
   both after the gate) request GMAIL_LABEL_SCOPES (readonly+modify).
   Red: the dry-run's factory saw [readonly, modify]; --apply saw one
   modify-scoped call and no readonly plan call.
2. WRONG RE-CONSENT MESSAGE: _consent_error now says
   `brain gmail-label --auth` (never `connectors auth email`, which is
   readonly and would change nothing). Red: message assertion.
3. UNDO HAS NO GATE: --undo sits behind the same _labeler_gate
   (exit 78, the re-consent message, ZERO Gmail calls) and then uses the
   modify-scoped client. Red: readonly-only token + --undo ran writes.
4. SMALL: token_grants_modify catches HTTPError/URLError/OSError from the
   token POST and raises GmailAuthError; the CLI gate turns it into a
   clean exit 78 - no traceback. Red: revoked token -> raw HTTPError.
5. SMALL: the --auth help and docstring state plainly that consent
   REPLACES the shared keychain refresh token the sync also uses (a
   superset, so the readonly sync keeps working).

Full suite 1711 passed / 4 skipped (brain_w3_labeler_test); ruff clean.
